  partName: Engine Block
  description: The Engine Block is the main structural component of the rocket engine,
    situated at the middle-center-center, and is constructed from a robust Moteur
    material. This large and complex-shaped part houses the engine's crankshaft,
    camshaft, and cylinders, making it a vital element in the engine's overall functionality.
    The Engine Block's size and material properties help to maintain the engine's
    stability and durability under extreme operating conditions.
